  type only inference can know -- the literal is the pair map it always was,
  byte for byte, and its definition CID does not move. If any does, the
  literal is a closed record: keyword keys only (`desugar-map` has already
  refused a mixed key kind by name), the key set closed, at most
  `max-record-fields` entries, fields in the same total order the pair map's
  entries are emitted in. A value that spells no type takes `:i64`, which is
  `:not-spelled :i64` from the typed-keyed literal applied unchanged, and is
  checked against that by `record-new`'s own inference afterwards.

